Write a function collatz_steps that takes an unsigned 32-bit number n (at least 1) and returns how
many steps the Collatz rule takes to reach 1: if n is even, n becomes n / 2, otherwise n becomes
3 * n + 1. collatz_steps(1) = 0. Intermediate values can exceed 32 bits; for every input checked the
answer is below 1000. It never traps for the inputs checked.
